    27	Failures and how to do differently:
    28	- Do not conflate internal WMS boxes, WB FBO box/pallet codes, FBS cargo places, FBS supply QR, and product barcodes.
    29	- Do not treat a transient SQLite `db_locked` failure as a code regression; reproduce the exact test, then rerun only the failed CI job on a clean runner.
    30	- Do not declare deployment complete from a running workflow; require migration completion, production smoke checks, and exact deployed SHA.
    31	
    32	Reusable knowledge:
    33	- Official WB FBW guidance found in the rollout says box/pallet codes are scanned at WB receiving, are unique per box/pallet, and may be ordinary barcode or QR. The code must be generated from WB-provided data; for third-party generation use only the dedicated third-party-print value.
    34	- Production deploy workflow validates trunk SHA, runs migrations, recreates services, and smoke-checks `/`, `/seller/`, and `/api/health`.
    35	- Final production evidence: all three endpoints returned HTTP 200; live FF and seller login pages loaded correctly. Post-deploy seller product imports emitted some WB 401 warnings, but these were unrelated to the barcode release.
    36	
    37	References:
    38	- Repository: `/Users/deniscivkunov/Projects/WMS`
    39	- PR: https://github.com/chivkunovd-bitdenis/WMS/pull/135
    40	- Merge SHA: `ce8f65abc31c91de65d7b082337d0a43f8dadd59`
    41	- Feature SHA: `4ebaa8e3e7f066caccf902500f04eac970d7104c`
    42	- Production workflow: https://github.com/chivkunovd-bitdenis/WMS/actions/runs/33034721763
    43	- Verification artifact: `/Users/deniscivkunov/Projects/WMS/.worktrees/wb-compatible-box-barcodes-20260826/docs/evidence/20260826-uvepen-po-formatu-modzhesh-sdelat-vezde-/backend-verification.md`
    44	
    45	## Task 2: Capture and structure the user’s follow-up backlog
    46	
    47	Outcome: partial
    48	
    49	Preference signals:
    50	- The user explicitly wants a separate BA/research agent to record and decompose dictated work into actionable tasks while implementation proceeds quickly in parallel.
    51	- The user strongly prefers additive, minimal, operator-focused UX rather than speculative redesign; for pallets they said the pallet is “просто агрегат” and should support fast drag-and-drop movement.
    52	- The user requires auditability for every operational action: creation, acceptance, status changes, packing, marking printing, shipment handoff, quantity edits, and all movements between cells, boxes, cargo places, and pallets.
    53	- Address storage is a global mode: when disabled, cell-related workflows should be hidden/disabled; undirected goods remain outside cells until explicitly sorted.
    54	- The user clarified that receiving comments and box/pallet free text are separate fields.
    55	
    56	Backlog requirements captured:
    57	- Research whether WB box SHKs are unique only within one shipment and whether self-generated duplicates can cause rejection or sanctions; use a separate inexpensive internet-research agent and official sources.
    58	- Receiving document: always show creation date immediately and after save; add a persistent free-text comment field beneath the main field.
    59	- Receiving/packing/shipment boxes: make the black barcode rendering about 20% brighter/less visually harsh; keep a separate CZ column rather than merging it into another column.
    60	- Cargo places should support adding goods; cargo places may represent a large box, bag, or package rather than only a conventional box.
    61	- Boxes and cargo places need a free-text field in their header. Printing their barcode must include seller, document/shipment number, date, quantity, and the free text in a lower label block. This applies consistently in receiving, shipment, and packing.
    62	- Boxes and cargo places need selection checkboxes. Selecting any combination exposes “Объединить в палету”; pallets are a higher-level aggregate with their own barcode, free text, expandable contents, print action, and ungroup/dissolve action.
    63	- Pallets must support fast drag-and-drop movement of boxes, cargo places, goods, and cell contents in any direction, with a quantity/weight confirmation capped by available quantity. Every movement must be logged.
    64	- Sorting must support creating/selecting cells via a medium-large modal listing all cells with warehouses, search, standard cell-label printing, and inline creation of a new cell with warehouse selection.
    65	- Sorting rows should be more visually distinct than the current light lavender. Verify goods can be assigned to cells before fully sorted; allow changing a cell even after packing approval, with re-approval and movement history.
    66	- Cell screen: expand a cell to see current products and boxes, using the standard product presentation (photo, seller, barcode, history).
    67	- FBS first tab: show a prominent but uncluttered average assembly time measured from order arrival in WMS until the operator presses shipment/delivery, not merely until packing.
    68	- Move FBS stock-allocation controls out of the FBS tab into the renamed “Товары” (currently Catalog) area. Per-product modal should use a 0–100% slider in 10% increments based on current free stock (physical stock minus reservations/pools, including FBS reservations), dynamically recalculated as stock changes.
    69	- Per-product allocation must include a global Wildberries sync checkbox and per-seller-WB-warehouse sliders. Global enabled means all warehouses sync; when disabled, warehouse controls become individually selectable. Show both percentages and current calculated quantities.
    70	- Bulk assignment: select multiple products, require one seller filter/selection, open the same modal, apply global and per-warehouse percentages to all selected products, then allow later per-product adjustment.
    71	
    72	Open status: the backlog was dictated and clarified but not yet decomposed into implemented task cards or code changes in this rollout.
    73	
    74	References:
    75	- Relevant WMS areas include `backend/app/services/warehouse_box_service.py`, `backend/app/services/inbound_intake_box_service.py`, `backend/app/services/marketplace_unload_box_service.py`, `frontend/src/screens/ff/FfSuppliesShipmentsPage.tsx`, `frontend/src/components/SellerMarketplaceUnloadDialog.tsx`, and `frontend/src/screens/v2/FfFbsSupplyWorkspace.tsx`.
    76	- Existing process notes distinguish `warehouse_boxes.internal_barcode`, FBO/FBW box/pallet SHK, FBS `supply_qr`, FBS `cargo_place_qr`, and product barcode; preserve those distinctions when creating follow-up cards.

